c expected: unsat
c
c x1 and not x1, written as two clauses on one line.  DIMACS ends a clause with
c 0 and separates its numbers with whitespace, so the layout carries no meaning
c and this is the same formula as the two-line version.  z3's own reader,
c `z3 -dimacs`, answers s UNSATISFIABLE.
c
c It answered sat on all three backends because the reader stripped only the
c LAST 0 of each line and took everything else for a literal: the line became one
c clause holding 1, -1 and a variable named 0 that the file never declares, which
c is a tautology.
p cnf 1 2
1 0 -1 0
